        {
          "type": "labelrows",
          "rows": [
            {
              "icon": "database",
              "label": "What it is:",
              "text": "split rows **horizontally** across independent servers (shards), each holding a subset"
            },
            {
              "icon": "server",
              "label": "Why it exists:",
              "text": "one machine eventually hits its write, storage, or memory limit"
            },
            {
              "icon": "network",
              "label": "Used for:",
              "text": "social feeds, messaging, and multi-tenant SaaS"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. How it works",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "user_id = 1001",
            "shard = hash(user_id) % 4",
            "# user 1001 -> shard 1"
          ],
          "note": "the shard key decides placement",
          "result": {
            "headers": [
              "user_id",
              "shard"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "1001",
                "1"
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Placement strategies",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Strategy",
            "Good",
            "Risk"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Hash of key",
              "even spread",
              "resharding"
            ],
            [
              "Range (A-F, G-M)",
              "range scans",
              "hot spots"
            ],
            [
              "Directory lookup",
              "flexible",
              "extra lookup service"
            ],
            [
              "Consistent hashing",
              "add shard, move ~1/N keys",
              "more complex"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Why bother",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Scales ==writes and storage== nearly linearly with shard count",
            "Faults stay contained: one shard down hurts only its users"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Watch out",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Cross-shard joins and transactions are slow or unsupported; need **two-phase commit** or app logic",
            "A bad shard key makes hot shards: a celebrity user, or sequential IDs on one shard",
            "Resharding is painful, so shard after indexing, replicas, and partitioning"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "banner",
          "title": "INTERVIEW TAKEAWAY:",
          "text": "Sharding is the last resort. Justify the shard key and name its cross-shard cost."
